%% Figure 5A — Lifecycle Action Processing
flowchart LR
  Actor([Authorized user]) --> UI[Fiori lifecycle action]
  UI --> Action[CAP bound action]
  Action --> Bug{Bug exists and current state\npermits this action?}
  Bug -- No --> NotFound[404/409 safe response\nNo mutation]
  Bug -- Yes --> Permission{Role, ownership and\nassignee checks pass?}
  Permission -- No --> Forbidden[403 denied\nNo mutation]
  Permission -- Yes --> Input{Required reason, note\nand assignee present?}
  Input -- No --> BadRequest[400 validation response\nNo mutation]
  Input -- Yes --> Transition{Allowed source-to-target\nstatus transition?}
  Transition -- No --> Conflict[400 validation response\nNo mutation]
  Transition -- Yes --> Patch[Build status, assignee and\nrejection-reason changes]
  Patch --> Owner[Determine next processor\nDeveloper, Tester or PM queue]
  Owner --> Transaction[(Single CAP transaction\nUpdate Bug and ownership)]
  Transaction --> History[Append HistoryEvent\nand field-level HistoryLogs]
  History --> Notify[Create applicable notification\nand email-delivery record]
  Notify --> Commit{Transaction\ncommitted?}
  Commit -- No --> Rollback[Rollback all database changes]
  Commit -- Yes --> Kick[Post-commit immediate email kick\nScheduler remains recovery]
  Kick --> Result([Return persisted Bug])

